Download VirtualBox from its official website. 
Run the installer and follow the setup wizard. 
Click install and complete the installation. 
Download the Ubuntu ISO file. 
Open VirtualBox and click New. 
Create a VM, name it, and select ISO file. 
Allocate RAM, CPU, and storage. 
Start the virtual machine and select install. 
Follow the on-screen installation. 
Create a user name and password. 
Complete the installation and restart the virtual machine.
